---
import { SITE } from "../../lib/format.mjs";
import { icon } from "../../lib/icons.mjs";
import { REPO } from "../../lib/html.mjs";
---

<section class="section help-home" id="help-build" aria-labelledby="hb-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2 id="hb-h">Help build this</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        {SITE.name} is open source. The code, the data pipeline and every method
        are public, and a correction from a reader is as useful as a fix from a
        programmer.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="doors">
      <article class="door">
        <h3>If you write code</h3>
        <p>
          Python for the pipeline, JavaScript for the site. It runs on a laptop
          with one command and no accounts, on a small sample of the records.
        </p>
        <p>
          <code class="cmd">
            git clone {REPO.replace("https://", "")} &amp;&amp; cd nl-ledger
            &amp;&amp; ./dev.sh
          </code>
        </p>
        <p>
          <a
            class="btn"
            href={
              REPO +
              "/issues?q=is%3Aopen+label%3A%22good+first+issue%22%2C%22help+wanted%22"
            }
          >
            Pick a starter issue <Fragment set:html={icon("arrow")} />
          </a>
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="door">
        <h3>If you do not</h3>
        <p>
          Know of public records the site is missing? Spot a figure that does
          not match its document? Think something is counted the wrong way? A
          link and a sentence is a full contribution.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a class="btn" href="/help/">
            See the four ways in <Fragment set:html={icon("arrow")} />
          </a>
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
    <p class="small muted">
      MIT licence. Every change is reviewed, and every figure must link to its
      source. <a href={REPO}>The repository on GitHub</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
